{"id": "EUVD-2026-106897", "enisaUuid": "66c80fbd-5253-3498-b72c-b7cbfcbbb756", "description": "Dulwich before 1.2.9 fails to validate DOS drive letter prefixes in Git tree path elements on Windows, allowing arbitrary file write. Attackers can craft a malicious repository with a tree entry named 'C:' that bypasses NTFS validation and writes files outside the worktree to achieve remote code execution.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T00:36:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T00:36:58", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/jelmer/dulwich/security/advisories/GHSA-8mcx-5rqc-vhmf", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/dulwich-before-1.2.9-arbitrary-file-write-via-dos-drive-letter-paths"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pxf3-54vf-v638", "CVE-2026-114094"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.67, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a2e753c9-b965-3f46-9834-4c24c3326b2e", "product": {"name": "dulwich", "vendor": {"name": "jelmer"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.2.9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "aa1ad989-4749-3571-939b-1b2c96a710b0", "vendor": {"name": "jelmer"}}], "isExploited": false}